From 7bf4c942e544165a1a6651afa795418114268f04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:13:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Operator proposer fees: L1 size from the real nonce and the
 signed maximum; operator fee bounded or the send is blocked

From custody-operator-proposal-20261023 1ac9ad2 (ROOT-FEE-FOLLOWUP).

- L1 data fee:
  - the size is computed from the EXACT transaction, including the real nonce
    (e.g. 23759, 2 bytes longer than the nonce 0 used before);
  - its maximum signed encoding is yParity 1, r = s = 2^256-1;
  - GasPriceOracle.getL1FeeUpperBound gets max(unsigned, signedMax-68), so the
    oracle's own +68 covers the signed transaction. Anything smaller refuses
    (l1_size); the old nonce-0 argument missed the signed maximum by 1 byte.
- Operator fee:
  - isIsthmus() must be true; getOperatorFee(gas limit) is the oracle's own
    computation, non-decreasing in gas used, at the agreed block on both RPCs;
  - otherwise (not Isthmus, a revert, RPC disagreement) the plan AND the send
    refuse (operator_fee): an undetermined fee blocks sending; no all-fee claim.
- fees.totalAtBlockWei = L2 cap + L1 bound + operator fee <= the unchanged
  0.000005 ETH cap; it replaces totalMaxWei. Balance is checked against it at
  send. These are bounds at the agreed block's oracle parameters, re-read at send.

The fixed target, caps, private journal, two-RPC agreement and pinned delegation
are unchanged. Tests 17/17 at 256 MiB; the unknown-outcome and journal tests are
unchanged. Mutants (nonce-0 sizing, operator fee dropped, undetermined fee as
zero) all fail the suite. FEE-NOTES.md is the file-only note for the canary fee
work. Nothing was signed, sent or funded.
